## 2026-08-19 — Task: Get IRS worksheet. Create test cases for the calculation.

- Fetched IRS Pub 915 (tax year 2025) Worksheet 1 "Figuring Your Taxable Benefits"
  from https://www.irs.gov/publications/p915 and saved it (lines 1-19 + the
  publication's worked example) to docs/irs-pub915-worksheet1-2025.md.
- Added a line-by-line reference implementation `pub915Worksheet1()` in
  src/utils/tax.test.ts (single filer, lines 4/5/7 = 0) and a new describe
  block "IRS Pub 915 Worksheet 1 (2025)" with:
  - the publication's worked example ($5,980 benefits + $28,990 other income
    -> $2,990 taxable), verified against both the reference and
    taxableSocialSecurity();
  - boundary cases at provisional income $25,000, $25,002, $34,000, $34,001;
  - an 8x11 grid cross-check (benefits 0..60k x incomes 0..100k) asserting
    taxableSocialSecurity() === worksheet result within 1e-8, reporting all
    mismatches at once.
- Existing taxableSocialSecurity() matched the worksheet on every case — no
  production-code changes needed.
- Discovered work (fixed): vite.config.ts used `defineConfig({...} as any)`,
  which failed eslint (no-explicit-any) and hid the `test` key from tsc.
  Switched to `import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config'` and dropped the
  cast. (First attempt via `/// <reference types="vitest/config" />` did not
  augment the type in vitest 4; the import does.)
- Verified: `npx tsc -b`, `npm run lint`, `npm test` (24 passed), `npm run build`
  all clean.

## 2026-08-19 — Task: Make SS benefit input a slider from 0 to max yearly SS benefit. Default to avg.

- Verified SSA 2025 figures via web search: max benefit claiming at age 70 is
  $5,108/mo -> $61,296/yr; average retired-worker benefit is $1,976/mo (Jan
  2025, after 2.5% COLA) -> $23,712/yr.
- Added MAX_ANNUAL_SS_BENEFIT (61,296) and AVG_ANNUAL_SS_BENEFIT (23,712)
  constants to src/utils/tax.ts with an SSA-sourced comment.
- App.tsx: replaced the number input with <input type="range"> min=0,
  max=MAX_ANNUAL_SS_BENEFIT, step=12 (keeps values on monthly-dollar
  boundaries, so both the avg default and the max are exact stops). Default
  state is now AVG_ANNUAL_SS_BENEFIT. Added a live currency readout next to
  the label and $0 / $61,296 (2025 max) endpoint labels under the track.
- index.css: range-specific overrides (the generic `input` rule's box
  padding/border looked wrong on a track): accent-color #38bdf8, transparent
  background, focus-visible outline; plus .slider-header/.slider-value/
  .slider-range-labels styles.
- App.test.tsx rewritten for the slider: role='slider', default value
  23712 + '$23,712' readout, min/max attributes, change -> value + readout
  update. Note: jest-dom toHaveValue returns a *string* for range inputs
  (only type=number coerces), so assertions compare strings.
- Verified: npx tsc -b, npm run lint, npm test (24 passed), npm run build
  all clean.

